# AD DS Fundamentals
## Lab Overview
Examine core components and structure of Active Directory Users and Computers
## Objectives
- Identify default OUs and Security Groups 
- Learn how to create/configure users and groups
- Navigate the hierarchical structure of AD DS
## Key Concepts
| Objects | configurable representations of persons or services in a network |
| Security Groups | defined collection of users, machines or other groups that grant varying access to network resources
| Organization Unit(OU) | containers that organize objects by structure and enable administration over sets of objects by means of GPOs | 
## Environment 
- Platform: TryHackMe.com VM
- OS: Windows Server 2019
- Directory Service: Active Directory
## Lab Walkthrogh
### Step 1 - Access Active Directory Users and Computers
Gives users an interactive view of the current and various domains, OU, child OUs, security groups and users
### Step 2 - Double-Click the OU named THM
Brought down a list of (5) child OUs that mimicked the organization of a business
### Step 3 - Left-Click on each of the child OUs
On the right panel of the screen it showed a list of the user objects in each child OU
### Step 4 - Right-Click on the OU named THM, hover over "new", Left-Click "Organizational Unit"
Allows provisioning of a child OU under THM
## Security Relevance
Objects and Security Groups should have least privilege princpals applied to critical resources and service in a Wndows Domain.
By applying least privilege it ensures that if service accounts are obtained malicioulsy the harm is mitigated
It is important that account passwords be of adequate length and complexity as well as changed periodically.
